<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Determine if the integral converges or diverges</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Calculate the integral below and determine if it converges or diverges</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{{@upper_lmt@}}\frac{{@num@}}{v}\,dv\)</p>
<p>First Integration \(=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>Second Integration \(=\)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>Therefore, the integral is [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>There is a discontinuity at \(v=0\)</p>
<p>So we split the integral </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{{@upper_lmt@}}\frac{{@num@}}{v}\,dv=\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{0}\frac{{@num@}}{v}\,dv=\displaystyle \int_{0}^{{@upper_lmt@}}\frac{{@num@}}{v}\,dv\)</p>
<p>Evaluate Each Part:</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle \int_{{@lower_lmt@}}^{0}\frac{{@num@}}{v}\,dv&=\displaystyle {@num@}\lim_{v \to t} \left( {@val1_upper@}-{@val1_lower@} \right)|_{@lower_lmt@}^{@t@}\\
&={@num@}({@ta1@})\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>Evaluating the other part of the integral</p>
<p>\(\begin{align}
\displaystyle \int_{0}^{{@upper_lmt@}}\frac{{@num@}}{v}\,dv&=\displaystyle {@num@}\lim_{v \to t} \left( {@val2_upper@}-{@val2_lower@} \right)|_{t}^{@upper_lmt@}\\
&={@num@}({@ta2@})\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<p> Since one part of the integral approaches \(-\infty \) and the other approaches \(+\infty \), the integral diverges.</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
